  "content": "elaine (Product Designer): morning \u2014 quick design review request for the on\u2011prem setup flow. I pushed a small prototype for a compact prereq summary + status pill approach. looking for copy + accessibility sanity checks. https://figma.com/file/xxxxxxxx\n\njosh (PM): saw the prototype \u2014 nice. +1 for collapsing logs by default. a few product Qs: do we show all network checks at once or group by category (dns/ports/credentials)?\n\nelaine (Product Designer): grouping by category feels cleaner and would help customers scan failures faster. proposal: show 3 pills across top (Network, Auth, Environment) with overall status, then an accordion per category with concise rows inside.\n\nsam (SRE): agree on grouping. one ask: the pill colors need to map to clear meanings and not rely on color only. current green/yellow/red is fine but we need text + icon. also add tooltip that explains remediation steps.\n\nkai (Frontend): noted. on implementation: pills will be <button> nodes for keyboard focus. we should expose aria-pressed or aria-expanded? pills are summary, accordion handles expansion. thinking aria-label like \"Network: passing (3 checks)\".\n\nelaine (Product Designer): good call \u2014 let's include explicit text inside the pill: e.g., \"Network \u2014 Passing\" and an icon. for collapsed state we show a microcopy line: \"All checks passed\" or \"2 failing\".\n\njosh (PM): microcopy suggestions: instead of \"failing\" use \"requires attention\" \u2014 less scary for users. also replace \"All checks passed\" with \"No action required\"? open to phrasing ideas.\n\nsam (SRE): prefer \"requires attention\" over \"failing\". \"No action required\" could be misread; maybe \"Ready to proceed\" is clearer for final step.\n\na11y-bot: accessibility note: ensure color contrast of pill background and text meets AA. If using icons, provide aria-hidden=\"true\" and a visible text label. For dynamic status updates, use an aria-live=\"polite\" region to announce changes for screen readers.\n\nkai (Frontend): will add aria-live region for the summary panel. suggest the following pattern for announcements:\n\n```\n<div aria-live=\"polite\">\n  Network: 2 checks passed, 1 requires attention\n</div>\n```\n\nelaine (Product Designer): thanks \u2014 can we make the announcement message friendlier? e.g., \"Network checks: 2 passed, 1 requires attention. See details.\"\n\njosh (PM): also let's ensure keyboard order is: pill row -> accordion headers -> first failing check action. avoid focus traps when logs expand.\n\nsam (SRE): logs should be collapsed and display a short excerpt line with a \"Show details\" button. When expanded, include a single copyable command snippet and link to a troubleshooting KB. avoid dumping full stack traces in default view.\n\nelaine (Product Designer): copy bank proposals:\n- Passing pill: \"Ready to proceed\"\n- Warning pill: \"Requires attention\"\n- Error pill: \"Action needed\"\n- Accordion row success line: \"Check passed\"\n- Row failure line: \"Check failed \u2014 see suggested fix\"\n\nkai (Frontend): small nit \u2014 use sentence case for microcopy to match rest of console. so \"Ready to proceed\" -> \"Ready to proceed\" (ok).\n\na11y-bot: confirm contrast for pill backgrounds at small sizes (>= 3:1 for large text, 4.5:1 for normal). keyboard focus should show a visible outline and not rely on color change alone.\n\njosh (PM): decision summary: group checks into category accordions, add status pills with explicit text + icon, use \"Requires attention\" wording for warnings, add aria-live announcements, collapse logs by default with a single copyable command and KB link. owners: kai to prototype accessibility pattern, sam to draft short KB snippets, elaine to update Figma copy.\n\nelaine (Product Designer): will update the file and ping when ready. tagging @kai and @sam for follow-ups. thanks all :raised_hands:\n\nkai (Frontend): i'll aim for a small PR with accessible pill component by EOD Thursday.\n\nsam (SRE): i'll author the KB steps and include a standard `diagnose.sh` snippet.\n\njosh (PM): perfect \u2014 capturing this in the ticket now. action items + ETA in the ticket.\n\nelaine (Product Designer): one more thing \u2014 think about mobile: switch pills to stacked horizontal scroll on small screens and make row tappable. we'll test in next usability pass.\n\nkai (Frontend): noted for responsive behavior.\n\na11y-bot: reminder: run axe-core once prototype is ready and post results in this thread.\n\nelaine (Product Designer): awesome, closing out for now. will post updated design link once done.",
